prompt:
Build ONE self-contained HTML file: an animated inline-4 four-stroke engine rendered on <canvas data-testid="simulation">. Exact kinematics (this is what gets graded): crank radius r = 45 mm, connecting-rod length l = 150 mm. Piston-pin height above the crankshaft axis for a cylinder whose throw is at crank angle theta is y(theta) = r*cos(theta) + sqrt(l*l - (r*sin(theta))^2) millimetres. Cylinders 1 and 4 ride the same throw (phase 0 deg); cylinders 2 and 3 ride the opposed throw (phase 180 deg). Crank angle is in degrees, rpm means revolutions per minute. RPM follows its target with first-order spool (time constant 0.5 s). Report crankDeg normalized to [0, 360); if the value is within 0.5 deg of 360, report 0. Draw the crankshaft, flywheel, four pistons with rods moving to the true kinematics, firing flashes in 1-3-4-2 order, plus a live readout of rpm, crank angle and piston heights.

MANDATORY benchmark API — a hidden automated grader calls exactly this; it must exist on window before load finishes, be deterministic for a given seed, and be independent of wall-clock time:
window.BENCH = {
  reset(seed) {},              // crank angle 0 deg, rpm 0, timeMs = 0
  step(ms) {},                 // advance by exactly ms milliseconds of simulated time using fixed-dt substeps (dt <= 0.001 s)
  perform(action, payload) {}, // 'throttle' with payload {rpm: number} sets the target rpm (0..6000)
  getState() { return {seed, timeMs, crankDeg, rpm}; },
  getMetrics() { return {timeMs, crankDeg, rpm, pistonY1, pistonY2, pistonY3, pistonY4}; }
};
pistonYk = piston-pin height in mm from the exact formula above (e.g. at crank 0 deg: cylinders 1 and 4 read 195 mm, cylinders 2 and 3 read 105 mm). Include <button data-testid="reset">Reset</button> wired to BENCH.reset(1). The scene must also animate via requestAnimationFrame during free viewing. No external libraries — plain canvas 2D and vanilla JS only. Use Math.cos / Math.sin (bare sin/cos do not exist in browsers).
